    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Matrix multiplication is a little more involved. We start by considering the dot product of two vectors, as this forms the basic operation of matrix multiplication. Letting a and b be two n-dimensional vectors (the first a column vector, the second a row vector), their dot product a · b is a scalar given by",
      "source_page": 200,
      "printed_page": 180,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter8:p008:b5"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        134.0,
